<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buôn Ma Thuột</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ban Me Thuot, Buon Ma Thuot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buôn Ma Thuột, known in the colonial period as Ban Me Thuot, is the main city of the Central Highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Under French rule it was the administrative centre of the highland Crown Domain, the Hoàng triều cương thổ, and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> plantations of Đắk Lắk. Its capture by North Vietnamese forces in March 1975 opened the offensive that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buon-ma-thuot.jpg" alt="Buôn Ma Thuột" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiyoshi Satou · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bmtcitycenter.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
